On GitHub → click “Use this template” → Create a new repository.

In the Firebase console, Add Your App --> Web App --> Copy the configuration and replace it in firebase.js 

Enable Auth, Firestore, Storage, Hosting. With Firestore and Storage, start in production mode.
Use git clone to clone the repository to your local machine 

From the command line, run npm install firebase (in your working directory) to add the Firebase JavaScript SDK to React project.

Run firebase init 
✔ Are you ready to proceed? Yes
✔ Which Firebase features do you want to set up for this directory? Press Space to select features, then Enter to confirm your choices.
Select firestore, storage, and hosting 

=== Project Setup
✔ Please select an option: Use an existing project

=== Firestore Setup
✔ What file should be used for Firestore Rules? firestore.rules
✔  What file should be used for Firestore indexes? firestore.indexes.json

=== Hosting Setup
✔ What do you want to use as your public directory? build
✔ Configure as a single-page app (rewrite all urls to /index.html)? Yes
✔ Set up automatic builds and deploys with GitHub? Yes
✔ For which GitHub repository would you like to set up a GitHub workflow?
(format: user/repository) 
✔ Set up the workflow to run a build script before every deploy? Yes
✔ What script should be run before every deploy? npm ci && npm run build
✔ Set up automatic deployment to your site's live channel when a PR is merged? Yes
✔ What is the name of the GitHub branch associated with your site's live channel? main

=== Storage Setup
✔ What file should be used for Storage Rules? storage.rules

Replace the Firestore and Storage rules in the local firestore.rules and storage.rules files with the rules provided in this README. 
Then run the following command to deploy the updated rules to Firebase:

firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
firebase deploy --only storage

This updates the rules in the Firebase Console to match the local rule files.

